- the request contains every token of exactly one column name as a contiguous phrase or a literal ('email addresses' → email_address, 'ip_country');
- the only pipeline that produced the delivered value selected a different column of that file by cut or awk index;
- nothing else fires, and there are no single-token matches.
In this sample that reaches formal-A-33 only, and it fires on no correct run (formal-A-57's f13 is a full match for 'IP addresses'). One run is not a reason to build. Run the offline replay (paid batch, pilot, pilot2, formal) and count distinct trajectories, not duplicate runs. Report how often it fires on accepted deliveries before spending anything live.

Keep it unbuilt. If it is ever revisited:
